window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/a402-09bc67d09f772585.json"]={sha256:"09bc67d09f772585a232f6f47c56a456ede7fbba0cf22097ee88c2dae709e300",value:{"id":"a402","title":"EUV 多層膜反射鏡","titleEn":"EUV multilayer mirrors","category":"instruments","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"從 EUV 強吸收出發，理解 Mo/Si 多層膜為何能反射、週期與粗糙度如何決定反射率，再把面形、鍍膜應力、污染、熱負載與波前誤差預算整合成可驗收的反射鏡工程。","summaryEn":"Start from strong EUV absorption to see why Mo/Si multilayers reflect, how period and roughness set reflectance, then integrate figure, coating stress, contamination, thermal load and wavefront budgets into an acceptable mirror engineering record.","scope":"依公開物理原理與官方資料編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是原廠配方、施工圖、設備操作許可或安全程序。數值均為教學假設，需依實際規格重算。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public physics and official sources. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not vendor recipes, construction drawings, operating authorisation or safety procedures. Numbers are teaching assumptions and must be recalculated for real specifications.","subcategory":"optics-lithography","subcategoryTitle":"微影光學與精密定位","subcategoryTitleEn":"Lithography optics and precision positioning","learningTrack":"optics","learningSubdiscipline":"optics-lithography","learningTags":["optics","optics-lithography","coating"],"architectureFamily":"coating","architectureNodes":[["EUV 光源與照明","EUV source and illumination"],["Mo/Si 多層膜堆","Mo/Si multilayer stack"],["超低膨脹基板","Ultralow-expansion substrate"],["Ru 覆蓋層與氫清潔","Ru cap and hydrogen cleaning"],["波前量測與對準","Wavefront metrology and alignment"],["晶圓像面","Wafer image plane"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[1,3],[1,4],[4,5]],"diagram":{"type":"coating","labels":["EUV 光源與照明","Mo/Si 多層膜堆","超低膨脹基板","Ru 覆蓋層與氫清潔","波前量測與對準"],"labelsEn":["EUV source and illumination","Mo/Si multilayer stack","Ultralow-expansion substrate","Ru cap and hydrogen cleaning","Wavefront metrology and alignment"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"波前預算練習：假設投影光學六片鏡子各分配 RMS 面形 0.15 nm、鍍膜 0.08 nm、對準 0.1 nm、熱漂移 0.1 nm。每片的面形貢獻為 2×0.15 = 0.30 nm；單鏡 RSS = √(0.30² + 0.08² + 0.10² + 0.10²) = 0.342 nm；六片 RSS = 0.342×√6 = 0.837 nm；Strehl ≈ exp[−(2π×0.837/13.5)²] = exp(−0.152) ≈ 0.86。若面形放寬到 0.25 nm，六片 RSS ≈ 1.29 nm，Strehl 降到約 0.70，低於 0.8 的常用判準。數值為教學假設，不代表任何實機規格。","textEn":"Wavefront-budget exercise: assume six projection mirrors, each allocated 0.15 nm RMS figure, 0.08 nm coating, 0.10 nm alignment and 0.10 nm thermal drift. Each mirror's figure contribution is 2×0.15 = 0.30 nm; the per-mirror RSS is √(0.30² + 0.08² + 0.10² + 0.10²) = 0.342 nm; six mirrors give 0.342×√6 = 0.837 nm; Strehl ≈ exp[−(2π×0.837/13.5)²] = exp(−0.152) ≈ 0.86. Relaxing figure to 0.25 nm raises the six-mirror RSS to about 1.29 nm and drops Strehl to about 0.70, below the common 0.8 criterion. Values are teaching assumptions, not any tool's specification.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表實機量測、產品額定或操作參數；改變系統邊界後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not measured hardware, product ratings or operating parameters; recalculate after changing the system boundary.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與設施背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and facility context, not these numbers."},"depth":4,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":12,"enrichmentVersion":12,"stages":[{"id":"a402-v12-s1","title":"系統邊界與物理原理","titleEn":"System boundaries and physical principles","description":"本階段聚焦「EUV 強吸收與反射式架構」與「多層膜週期與布拉格條件」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Strong EUV absorption and the reflective architecture\" and \"Multilayer period and the Bragg condition\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a402-v12-01","title":"EUV 強吸收與反射式架構：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Strong EUV absorption and the reflective architecture: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「反射式光路與真空腔」如何決定EUV 多層膜反射鏡的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Reflective optical path and vacuum chamber” determines the key performance of “EUV multilayer mirrors”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"在 13.5 nm 波長，所有固體材料的折射率都非常接近 1 且吸收係數很大，折射率可寫成 n = 1 − δ + iβ，δ 與 β 都只有百分之幾或更小；光在數十奈米內就被吸收，所以不能用透鏡折射成像，整個光路必須放在真空中並以多層膜反射鏡轉折與聚焦。空氣本身也會吸收 EUV，因此照明、光罩與投影光學都在真空腔內。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「反射式光路與真空腔」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"At 13.5 nm every solid has a refractive index very close to 1 with strong absorption; writing n = 1 − δ + iβ, both δ and β are a few percent or less, and the light is absorbed within tens of nanometers. Refractive lenses therefore cannot image EUV, so the whole optical train is folded and focused by multilayer mirrors inside a vacuum chamber, because air itself absorbs EUV as well. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Reflective optical path and vacuum chamber”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：單一界面的正向反射率約為 R ≈ |(n₁ − n₂)/(n₁ + n₂)|²；當 δ 只有 0.01 量級時，單一界面反射率僅約 10⁻⁴ 到 10⁻³ 等級，只有把數十個界面以相同相位疊加才能得到可用的反射率。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A single interface reflects roughly R ≈ |(n₁ − n₂)/(n₁ + n₂)|² at normal incidence; with δ of order 0.01 that is only 10⁻⁴ to 10⁻³, so a usable reflectance needs tens of interfaces adding in phase.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要材料夠純、夠透明，EUV 也能像 DUV 一樣用透鏡成像。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"With pure enough transparent material, EUV could be imaged with lenses like DUV.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「反射式光路與真空腔」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Reflective optical path and vacuum chamber”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-01-k1","title":"EUV 強吸收與反射式架構","titleEn":"Strong EUV absorption and the reflective architecture","text":"在 13.5 nm 波長，所有固體材料的折射率都非常接近 1 且吸收係數很大，折射率可寫成 n = 1 − δ + iβ，δ 與 β 都只有百分之幾或更小；光在數十奈米內就被吸收，所以不能用透鏡折射成像，整個光路必須放在真空中並以多層膜反射鏡轉折與聚焦。空氣本身也會吸收 EUV，因此照明、光罩與投影光學都在真空腔內。","textEn":"At 13.5 nm every solid has a refractive index very close to 1 with strong absorption; writing n = 1 − δ + iβ, both δ and β are a few percent or less, and the light is absorbed within tens of nanometers. Refractive lenses therefore cannot image EUV, so the whole optical train is folded and focused by multilayer mirrors inside a vacuum chamber, because air itself absorbs EUV as well.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要材料夠純、夠透明，EUV 也能像 DUV 一樣用透鏡成像。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: With pure enough transparent material, EUV could be imaged with lenses like DUV. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「EUV 強吸收與反射式架構」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Strong EUV absorption and the reflective architecture\" is correct?","options":["只要材料夠純、夠透明，EUV 也能像 DUV 一樣用透鏡成像。","在 13.5 nm 波長，所有固體材料的折射率都非常接近 1 且吸收係數很大，折射率可寫成 n = 1 − δ + iβ，δ 與 β 都只有百分之幾或更小。","雙層數越多，反射率一定越高。"],"optionsEn":["With pure enough transparent material, EUV could be imaged with lenses like DUV.","At 13.5 nm every solid has a refractive index very close to 1 with strong absorption.","More bilayers always give higher reflectance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在 13.5 nm 波長，所有固體材料的折射率都非常接近 1 且吸收係數很大，折射率可寫成 n = 1 − δ + iβ，δ 與 β 都只有百分之幾或更小；光在數十奈米內就被吸收，所以不能用透鏡折射成像，整個光路必須放在真空中並以多層膜反射鏡轉折與聚焦。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"At 13.5 nm every solid has a refractive index very close to 1 with strong absorption; writing n = 1 − δ + iβ, both δ and β are a few percent or less, and the light is absorbed within tens of nanometers. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"a402-v12-02","title":"EUV 強吸收與反射式架構：定量估算","titleEn":"Strong EUV absorption and the reflective architecture: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「反射式光路與真空腔」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Reflective optical path and vacuum chamber” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：單一界面的正向反射率約為 R ≈ |(n₁ − n₂)/(n₁ + n₂)|²；當 δ 只有 0.01 量級時，單一界面反射率僅約 10⁻⁴ 到 10⁻³ 等級，只有把數十個界面以相同相位疊加才能得到可用的反射率。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A single interface reflects roughly R ≈ |(n₁ − n₂)/(n₁ + n₂)|² at normal incidence; with δ of order 0.01 that is only 10⁻⁴ to 10⁻³, so a usable reflectance needs tens of interfaces adding in phase. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：以公開的光學常數資料庫（例如 CXRO）查 Mo 與 Si 在 13.5 nm 的 δ、β，計算單界面反射率與 1/e 吸收深度，並與多層膜的實測反射率曲線比較，確認差了兩到三個數量級。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Look up δ and β of Mo and Si at 13.5 nm from a public optical-constants database such as CXRO, compute the single-interface reflectance and the 1/e absorption depth, and compare with a measured multilayer reflectance curve to confirm the two-to-three-order-of-magnitude gap.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"單一界面的正向反射率約為 R ≈ |(n₁ − n₂)/(n₁ + n₂)|²；當 δ 只有 0.01 量級時，單一界面反射率僅約 10⁻⁴ 到 10⁻³ 等級，只有把數十個界面以相同相位疊加才能得到可用的反射率。","textEn":"A single interface reflects roughly R ≈ |(n₁ − n₂)/(n₁ + n₂)|² at normal incidence; with δ of order 0.01 that is only 10⁻⁴ to 10⁻³, so a usable reflectance needs tens of interfaces adding in phase.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「EUV 強吸收與反射式架構」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Strong EUV absorption and the reflective architecture\", which statement holds?","options":["基板很厚時，幾百奈米薄膜的應力可以忽略。","λ/4 的面形品質對任何波長都是「繞射極限」。","單一界面的正向反射率約為 R ≈ |(n₁ − n₂)/(n₁ + n₂)|²。"],"optionsEn":["For a thick substrate the stress of a few hundred nanometres of film is negligible.","λ/4 figure quality is diffraction limited at any wavelength.","A single interface reflects roughly R ≈ |(n₁ − n₂)/(n₁ + n₂)|² at normal incidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"單一界面的正向反射率約為 R ≈ |(n₁ − n₂)/(n₁ + n₂)|²；當 δ 只有 0.01 量級時，單一界面反射率僅約 10⁻⁴ 到 10⁻³ 等級，只有把數十個界面以相同相位疊加才能得到可用的反射率。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A single interface reflects roughly R ≈ |(n₁ − n₂)/(n₁ + n₂)|² at normal incidence; with δ of order 0.01 that is only 10⁻⁴ to 10⁻³, so a usable reflectance needs tens of interfaces adding in phase. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"a402-v12-03","title":"EUV 強吸收與反射式架構：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Strong EUV absorption and the reflective architecture: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「反射式光路與真空腔」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Reflective optical path and vacuum chamber” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"以公開的光學常數資料庫（例如 CXRO）查 Mo 與 Si 在 13.5 nm 的 δ、β，計算單界面反射率與 1/e 吸收深度，並與多層膜的實測反射率曲線比較，確認差了兩到三個數量級。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Look up δ and β of Mo and Si at 13.5 nm from a public optical-constants database such as CXRO, compute the single-interface reflectance and the 1/e absorption depth, and compare with a measured multilayer reflectance curve to confirm the two-to-three-order-of-magnitude gap. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：若把 DUV 的折射式鏡頭觀念套到 EUV，會估出根本不存在的透鏡光路；真實失效是光在元件內被吸收而沒有能量到達晶圓，系統通量不足。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Carrying DUV refractive-lens thinking into EUV produces a lens train that cannot exist; the real failure is light absorbed inside the element so that throughput at the wafer collapses.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以公開的光學常數資料庫（例如 CXRO）查 Mo 與 Si 在 13.5 nm 的 δ、β，計算單界面反射率與 1/e 吸收深度，並與多層膜的實測反射率曲線比較，確認差了兩到三個數量級。","textEn":"Look up δ and β of Mo and Si at 13.5 nm from a public optical-constants database such as CXRO, compute the single-interface reflectance and the 1/e absorption depth, and compare with a measured multilayer reflectance curve to confirm the two-to-three-order-of-magnitude gap.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-03-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「EUV 強吸收與反射式架構」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Strong EUV absorption and the reflective architecture\"?","options":["以公開的光學常數資料庫（例如 CXRO）查 Mo 與 Si 在 13.5 nm 的 δ、β，計算單界面反射率與 1/e 吸收深度，並與多層膜的實測反射率曲線比較，確認差了兩到三個數量級。","量測時不必記錄溫度、振動與時間等條件，因為它們不會影響結果。","超低膨脹材料就表示熱變形為零。"],"optionsEn":["Look up δ and β of Mo and Si at 13.5 nm from a public optical-constants database such as CXRO, compute the single-interface reflectance and the 1/e absorption depth, and compare with a measured multilayer reflectance curve to confirm the two-to-three-order-of-magnitude gap.","Temperature, vibration and timing need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Ultralow-expansion material means zero thermal deformation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以公開的光學常數資料庫（例如 CXRO）查 Mo 與 Si 在 13.5 nm 的 δ、β，計算單界面反射率與 1/e 吸收深度，並與多層膜的實測反射率曲線比較，確認差了兩到三個數量級。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Look up δ and β of Mo and Si at 13.5 nm from a public optical-constants database such as CXRO, compute the single-interface reflectance and the 1/e absorption depth, and compare with a measured multilayer reflectance curve to confirm the two-to-three-order-of-magnitude gap. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"a402-v12-04","title":"EUV 強吸收與反射式架構：失效診斷","titleEn":"Strong EUV absorption and the reflective architecture: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「反射式光路與真空腔」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Reflective optical path and vacuum chamber” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"若把 DUV 的折射式鏡頭觀念套到 EUV，會估出根本不存在的透鏡光路；真實失效是光在元件內被吸收而沒有能量到達晶圓，系統通量不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Carrying DUV refractive-lens thinking into EUV produces a lens train that cannot exist; the real failure is light absorbed inside the element so that throughput at the wafer collapses. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：空氣本身也會吸收 EUV，因此照明、光罩與投影光學都在真空腔內。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Refractive lenses therefore cannot image EUV, so the whole optical train is folded and focused by multilayer mirrors inside a vacuum chamber, because air itself absorbs EUV as well.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要材料夠純、夠透明，EUV 也能像 DUV 一樣用透鏡成像。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"With pure enough transparent material, EUV could be imaged with lenses like DUV.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若把 DUV 的折射式鏡頭觀念套到 EUV，會估出根本不存在的透鏡光路；真實失效是光在元件內被吸收而沒有能量到達晶圓，系統通量不足。","textEn":"Carrying DUV refractive-lens thinking into EUV produces a lens train that cannot exist; the real failure is light absorbed inside the element so that throughput at the wafer collapses.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「EUV 強吸收與反射式架構」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Strong EUV absorption and the reflective architecture\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自操作人員失誤，系統設計不需要檢討。","若把 DUV 的折射式鏡頭觀念套到 EUV，會估出根本不存在的透鏡光路；真實失效是光在元件內被吸收而沒有能量到達晶圓，系統通量不足。","雙層數越多，反射率一定越高。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is operator error, so the system design never needs review.","Carrying DUV refractive-lens thinking into EUV produces a lens train that cannot exist.","More bilayers always give higher reflectance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若把 DUV 的折射式鏡頭觀念套到 EUV，會估出根本不存在的透鏡光路；真實失效是光在元件內被吸收而沒有能量到達晶圓，系統通量不足。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Carrying DUV refractive-lens thinking into EUV produces a lens train that cannot exist; the real failure is light absorbed inside the element so that throughput at the wafer collapses. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"a402-v12-05","title":"多層膜週期與布拉格條件：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Multilayer period and the Bragg condition: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-04"],"objective":"說明「Mo/Si 多層膜堆」如何決定EUV 多層膜反射鏡的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Mo/Si multilayer stack” determines the key performance of “EUV multilayer mirrors”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"Mo/Si 多層膜由約 40 到 50 組雙層構成，每組週期 d 約 6.9 nm，Mo 約佔週期的 0.4。各界面的微弱反射在正向入射時因為光程差等於一個波長而同相疊加，形成類似布拉格繞射的反射峰；由於材料吸收，週期數超過約 50 組後反射率不再提升。理論峰值約 74%，實際鍍膜約 70%。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「Mo/Si 多層膜堆」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A Mo/Si multilayer has about 40 to 50 bilayers with a period d of roughly 6.9 nm and a molybdenum fraction near 0.4. The weak reflections from each interface add in phase at normal incidence because the round-trip path equals one wavelength, giving a Bragg-like reflectance peak; absorption makes additional bilayers beyond about 50 useless. The theoretical peak is about 74% and production coatings reach about 70%. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Mo/Si multilayer stack”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：修正折射後的布拉格條件為 mλ = 2d·sinθ·√(1 − 2δ̄/sin²θ)，其中 δ̄ 是週期平均的 δ；在正向入射（θ = 90°）、m = 1、λ = 13.5 nm、δ̄ ≈ 0.02 時，d ≈ λ/(2√(1 − 2δ̄)) ≈ 6.89 nm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The refraction-corrected Bragg condition is mλ = 2d·sinθ·√(1 − 2δ̄/sin²θ) with δ̄ the period-averaged δ; at normal incidence, m = 1, λ = 13.5 nm and δ̄ ≈ 0.02, d ≈ λ/(2√(1 − 2δ̄)) ≈ 6.89 nm.","failure":"常見誤解：「雙層數越多，反射率一定越高。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"More bilayers always give higher reflectance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「Mo/Si 多層膜堆」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Mo/Si multilayer stack”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-05-k1","title":"多層膜週期與布拉格條件","titleEn":"Multilayer period and the Bragg condition","text":"Mo/Si 多層膜由約 40 到 50 組雙層構成，每組週期 d 約 6.9 nm，Mo 約佔週期的 0.4。各界面的微弱反射在正向入射時因為光程差等於一個波長而同相疊加，形成類似布拉格繞射的反射峰；由於材料吸收，週期數超過約 50 組後反射率不再提升。","textEn":"A Mo/Si multilayer has about 40 to 50 bilayers with a period d of roughly 6.9 nm and a molybdenum fraction near 0.4. The weak reflections from each interface add in phase at normal incidence because the round-trip path equals one wavelength, giving a Bragg-like reflectance peak; absorption makes additional bilayers beyond about 50 useless.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：雙層數越多，反射率一定越高。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: More bilayers always give higher reflectance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「多層膜週期與布拉格條件」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Multilayer period and the Bragg condition\" is correct?","options":["雙層數越多，反射率一定越高。","達到可見光光學的光滑度，對 EUV 也足夠。","Mo/Si 多層膜由約 40 到 50 組雙層構成，每組週期 d 約 6.9 nm，Mo 約佔週期的 0.4。"],"optionsEn":["More bilayers always give higher reflectance.","A surface smooth enough for visible optics is smooth enough for EUV.","A Mo/Si multilayer has about 40 to 50 bilayers with a period d of roughly 6.9 nm and a molybdenum fraction near 0.4."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Mo/Si 多層膜由約 40 到 50 組雙層構成，每組週期 d 約 6.9 nm，Mo 約佔週期的 0.4。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A Mo/Si multilayer has about 40 to 50 bilayers with a period d of roughly 6.9 nm and a molybdenum fraction near 0.4. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"a402-v12-06","title":"多層膜週期與布拉格條件：定量估算","titleEn":"Multilayer period and the Bragg condition: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「Mo/Si 多層膜堆」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Mo/Si multilayer stack” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：修正折射後的布拉格條件為 mλ = 2d·sinθ·√(1 − 2δ̄/sin²θ)，其中 δ̄ 是週期平均的 δ；在正向入射（θ = 90°）、m = 1、λ = 13.5 nm、δ̄ ≈ 0.02 時，d ≈ λ/(2√(1 − 2δ̄)) ≈ 6.89 nm。週期誤差會按 Δλ/λ ≈ Δd/d 推移峰值波長。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The refraction-corrected Bragg condition is mλ = 2d·sinθ·√(1 − 2δ̄/sin²θ) with δ̄ the period-averaged δ; at normal incidence, m = 1, λ = 13.5 nm and δ̄ ≈ 0.02, d ≈ λ/(2√(1 − 2δ̄)) ≈ 6.89 nm. A period error shifts the peak by Δλ/λ ≈ Δd/d. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：用布拉格式算出目標週期後，與同步輻射反射率計（例如 PTB 在 BESSY II 的 EUV 反射率量測）給出的峰值波長與頻寬比較；再改變週期 ±1% 預測峰值位移約 ±0.14 nm，與量測比對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: After computing the target period from the Bragg relation, compare with the peak wavelength and bandwidth from synchrotron reflectometry such as the PTB EUV reflectometry at BESSY II; then perturb the period by ±1%, predict a peak shift of about ±0.14 nm and check against measurement.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"修正折射後的布拉格條件為 mλ = 2d·sinθ·√(1 − 2δ̄/sin²θ)，其中 δ̄ 是週期平均的 δ；在正向入射（θ = 90°）、m = 1、λ = 13.5 nm、δ̄ ≈ 0.02 時，d ≈ λ/(2√(1 − 2δ̄)) ≈ 6.89 nm。週期誤差會按 Δλ/λ ≈ Δd/d 推移峰值波長。","textEn":"The refraction-corrected Bragg condition is mλ = 2d·sinθ·√(1 − 2δ̄/sin²θ) with δ̄ the period-averaged δ; at normal incidence, m = 1, λ = 13.5 nm and δ̄ ≈ 0.02, d ≈ λ/(2√(1 − 2δ̄)) ≈ 6.89 nm. A period error shifts the peak by Δλ/λ ≈ Δd/d.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「多層膜週期與布拉格條件」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Multilayer period and the Bragg condition\", which statement holds?","options":["修正折射後的布拉格條件為 mλ = 2d·sinθ·√(1 − 2δ̄/sin²θ)，其中 δ̄ 是週期平均的 δ。","在真空中工作的鏡面不會受到污染。","超低膨脹材料就表示熱變形為零。"],"optionsEn":["The refraction-corrected Bragg condition is mλ = 2d·sinθ·√(1 − 2δ̄/sin²θ) with δ̄ the period-averaged δ.","A mirror working in vacuum cannot get contaminated.","Ultralow-expansion material means zero thermal deformation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"修正折射後的布拉格條件為 mλ = 2d·sinθ·√(1 − 2δ̄/sin²θ)，其中 δ̄ 是週期平均的 δ；在正向入射（θ = 90°）、m = 1、λ = 13.5 nm、δ̄ ≈ 0.02 時，d ≈ λ/(2√(1 − 2δ̄)) ≈ 6.89 nm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The refraction-corrected Bragg condition is mλ = 2d·sinθ·√(1 − 2δ̄/sin²θ) with δ̄ the period-averaged δ; at normal incidence, m = 1, λ = 13.5 nm and δ̄ ≈ 0.02, d ≈ λ/(2√(1 − 2δ̄)) ≈ 6.89 nm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"a402-v12-07","title":"多層膜週期與布拉格條件：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Multilayer period and the Bragg condition: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「Mo/Si 多層膜堆」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Mo/Si multilayer stack” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"用布拉格式算出目標週期後，與同步輻射反射率計（例如 PTB 在 BESSY II 的 EUV 反射率量測）給出的峰值波長與頻寬比較；再改變週期 ±1% 預測峰值位移約 ±0.14 nm，與量測比對。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"After computing the target period from the Bragg relation, compare with the peak wavelength and bandwidth from synchrotron reflectometry such as the PTB EUV reflectometry at BESSY II; then perturb the period by ±1%, predict a peak shift of about ±0.14 nm and check against measurement. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：界面互擴散形成 MoSi₂ 會讓有效界面變寬、反射率下降；週期沿鏡面漸變若與設計的入射角分佈不符，鏡面不同位置的峰值波長會錯開，整鏡反射率與均勻性同時變差。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Interdiffusion that forms MoSi₂ broadens the effective interface and lowers reflectance; if the lateral period gradient does not match the designed angle-of-incidence map, different mirror zones peak at different wavelengths and both reflectance and uniformity degrade.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用布拉格式算出目標週期後，與同步輻射反射率計（例如 PTB 在 BESSY II 的 EUV 反射率量測）給出的峰值波長與頻寬比較；再改變週期 ±1% 預測峰值位移約 ±0.14 nm，與量測比對。","textEn":"After computing the target period from the Bragg relation, compare with the peak wavelength and bandwidth from synchrotron reflectometry such as the PTB EUV reflectometry at BESSY II; then perturb the period by ±1%, predict a peak shift of about ±0.14 nm and check against measurement.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-07-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「多層膜週期與布拉格條件」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Multilayer period and the Bragg condition\"?","options":["沿用另一台設備或另一個案例的量測結果，就可視為本系統已完成驗證。","用布拉格式算出目標週期後，與同步輻射反射率計（例如 PTB 在 BESSY II 的 EUV 反射率量測）給出的峰值波長與頻寬比較。","每片鏡子都通過驗收，整組光學就自動合格。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another instrument or another case counts as verifying this system.","After computing the target period from the Bragg relation, compare with the peak wavelength and bandwidth from synchrotron reflectometry such as the PTB EUV reflectometry at BESSY II.","If every mirror passes, the assembled optics automatically pass."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用布拉格式算出目標週期後，與同步輻射反射率計（例如 PTB 在 BESSY II 的 EUV 反射率量測）給出的峰值波長與頻寬比較；再改變週期 ±1% 預測峰值位移約 ±0.14 nm，與量測比對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"After computing the target period from the Bragg relation, compare with the peak wavelength and bandwidth from synchrotron reflectometry such as the PTB EUV reflectometry at BESSY II; then perturb the period by ±1%, predict a peak shift of about ±0.14 nm and check against measurement. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"a402-v12-08","title":"多層膜週期與布拉格條件：失效診斷","titleEn":"Multilayer period and the Bragg condition: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「Mo/Si 多層膜堆」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Mo/Si multilayer stack” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"界面互擴散形成 MoSi₂ 會讓有效界面變寬、反射率下降；週期沿鏡面漸變若與設計的入射角分佈不符，鏡面不同位置的峰值波長會錯開，整鏡反射率與均勻性同時變差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Interdiffusion that forms MoSi₂ broadens the effective interface and lowers reflectance; if the lateral period gradient does not match the designed angle-of-incidence map, different mirror zones peak at different wavelengths and both reflectance and uniformity degrade. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：理論峰值約 74%，實際鍍膜約 70%。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The theoretical peak is about 74% and production coatings reach about 70%.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「雙層數越多，反射率一定越高。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"More bilayers always give higher reflectance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"界面互擴散形成 MoSi₂ 會讓有效界面變寬、反射率下降；週期沿鏡面漸變若與設計的入射角分佈不符，鏡面不同位置的峰值波長會錯開，整鏡反射率與均勻性同時變差。","textEn":"Interdiffusion that forms MoSi₂ broadens the effective interface and lowers reflectance; if the lateral period gradient does not match the designed angle-of-incidence map, different mirror zones peak at different wavelengths and both reflectance and uniformity degrade.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「多層膜週期與布拉格條件」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Multilayer period and the Bragg condition\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["調高增益或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數異常。","達到可見光光學的光滑度，對 EUV 也足夠。","界面互擴散形成 MoSi₂ 會讓有效界面變寬、反射率下降；週期沿鏡面漸變若與設計的入射角分佈不符，鏡面不同位置的峰值波長會錯開，整鏡反射率與均勻性同時變差。"],"optionsEn":["Raising the gain or widening the acceptance limits solves most anomalies.","A surface smooth enough for visible optics is smooth enough for EUV.","Interdiffusion that forms MoSi₂ broadens the effective interface and lowers reflectance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"界面互擴散形成 MoSi₂ 會讓有效界面變寬、反射率下降；週期沿鏡面漸變若與設計的入射角分佈不符，鏡面不同位置的峰值波長會錯開，整鏡反射率與均勻性同時變差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Interdiffusion that forms MoSi₂ broadens the effective interface and lowers reflectance; if the lateral period gradient does not match the designed angle-of-incidence map, different mirror zones peak at different wavelengths and both reflectance and uniformity degrade. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"a402-v12-s2","title":"元件、材料與製造","titleEn":"Components, materials and fabrication","description":"本階段聚焦「面形誤差、中高頻粗糙度與散射」與「鍍膜製程與多層膜應力」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Figure error, mid/high-spatial-frequency roughness and scatter\" and \"Deposition process and multilayer stress\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a402-v12-09","title":"面形誤差、中高頻粗糙度與散射：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Figure error, mid/high-spatial-frequency roughness and scatter: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-08"],"objective":"說明「基板面形與粗糙度頻譜」如何決定EUV 多層膜反射鏡的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Substrate figure and roughness spectrum” determines the key performance of “EUV multilayer mirrors”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"鏡面誤差依空間頻率分成三段：低頻的面形誤差直接變成波前像差；中頻粗糙度（MSFR）把光散射到像點附近形成眩光（flare），降低影像對比；高頻粗糙度（HSFR）把光散射到視場之外，等效降低反射率。因為波長只有 13.5 nm，可接受的粗糙度是 0.1 nm 等級，比可見光光學嚴格兩個數量級。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「基板面形與粗糙度頻譜」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Mirror errors are split by spatial frequency: low-frequency figure error becomes wavefront aberration; mid-spatial-frequency roughness (MSFR) scatters light near the image point as flare that reduces contrast; high-spatial-frequency roughness (HSFR) scatters light out of the field and acts like a reflectance loss. Because the wavelength is only 13.5 nm, acceptable roughness is of order 0.1 nm, two orders of magnitude tighter than visible optics. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Substrate figure and roughness spectrum”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：總積分散射近似為 TIS ≈ (4π·σ·cosθ/λ)²；取 σ = 0.1 nm、正向入射、λ = 13.5 nm，TIS ≈ (4π×0.1/13.5)² ≈ 0.0087，即約 0.9% 的光被散射；σ = 0.2 nm 時約 3.5%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Total integrated scatter is approximately TIS ≈ (4π·σ·cosθ/λ)²; with σ = 0.1 nm at normal incidence and λ = 13.5 nm, TIS ≈ (4π×0.1/13.5)² ≈ 0.0087, about 0.9% of the light, and about 3.5% for σ = 0.2 nm.","failure":"常見誤解：「達到可見光光學的光滑度，對 EUV 也足夠。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A surface smooth enough for visible optics is smooth enough for EUV.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「基板面形與粗糙度頻譜」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Substrate figure and roughness spectrum”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-09-k1","title":"面形誤差、中高頻粗糙度與散射","titleEn":"Figure error, mid/high-spatial-frequency roughness and scatter","text":"鏡面誤差依空間頻率分成三段：低頻的面形誤差直接變成波前像差；中頻粗糙度（MSFR）把光散射到像點附近形成眩光（flare），降低影像對比；高頻粗糙度（HSFR）把光散射到視場之外，等效降低反射率。因為波長只有 13.5 nm，可接受的粗糙度是 0.1 nm 等級，比可見光光學嚴格兩個數量級。","textEn":"Mirror errors are split by spatial frequency: low-frequency figure error becomes wavefront aberration; mid-spatial-frequency roughness (MSFR) scatters light near the image point as flare that reduces contrast; high-spatial-frequency roughness (HSFR) scatters light out of the field and acts like a reflectance loss. Because the wavelength is only 13.5 nm, acceptable roughness is of order 0.1 nm, two orders of magnitude tighter than visible optics.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：達到可見光光學的光滑度，對 EUV 也足夠。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A surface smooth enough for visible optics is smooth enough for EUV. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「面形誤差、中高頻粗糙度與散射」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Figure error, mid/high-spatial-frequency roughness and scatter\" is correct?","options":["鏡面誤差依空間頻率分成三段：低頻的面形誤差直接變成波前像差。","達到可見光光學的光滑度，對 EUV 也足夠。","基板很厚時，幾百奈米薄膜的應力可以忽略。"],"optionsEn":["Mirror errors are split by spatial frequency: low-frequency figure error becomes wavefront aberration.","A surface smooth enough for visible optics is smooth enough for EUV.","For a thick substrate the stress of a few hundred nanometres of film is negligible."],"answer":0,"explanation":"鏡面誤差依空間頻率分成三段：低頻的面形誤差直接變成波前像差；中頻粗糙度（MSFR）把光散射到像點附近形成眩光（flare），降低影像對比；高頻粗糙度（HSFR）把光散射到視場之外，等效降低反射率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Mirror errors are split by spatial frequency: low-frequency figure error becomes wavefront aberration; mid-spatial-frequency roughness (MSFR) scatters light near the image point as flare that reduces contrast; high-spatial-frequency roughness (HSFR) scatters light out of the field and acts like a reflectance loss. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"a402-v12-10","title":"面形誤差、中高頻粗糙度與散射：定量估算","titleEn":"Figure error, mid/high-spatial-frequency roughness and scatter: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「基板面形與粗糙度頻譜」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Substrate figure and roughness spectrum” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：總積分散射近似為 TIS ≈ (4π·σ·cosθ/λ)²；取 σ = 0.1 nm、正向入射、λ = 13.5 nm，TIS ≈ (4π×0.1/13.5)² ≈ 0.0087，即約 0.9% 的光被散射；σ = 0.2 nm 時約 3.5%。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Total integrated scatter is approximately TIS ≈ (4π·σ·cosθ/λ)²; with σ = 0.1 nm at normal incidence and λ = 13.5 nm, TIS ≈ (4π×0.1/13.5)² ≈ 0.0087, about 0.9% of the light, and about 3.5% for σ = 0.2 nm. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：以干涉儀量面形、以白光干涉或 AFM 量不同取樣長度的粗糙度，將功率譜密度（PSD）依頻段積分成三個 σ 值，再用 TIS 公式估散射損失並與反射率量測差額比對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure figure with an interferometer and roughness at several sampling lengths with white-light interferometry or AFM, integrate the power spectral density into three band-limited σ values, then estimate scatter loss with the TIS relation and compare with the reflectance shortfall.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"總積分散射近似為 TIS ≈ (4π·σ·cosθ/λ)²；取 σ = 0.1 nm、正向入射、λ = 13.5 nm，TIS ≈ (4π×0.1/13.5)² ≈ 0.0087，即約 0.9% 的光被散射；σ = 0.2 nm 時約 3.5%。","textEn":"Total integrated scatter is approximately TIS ≈ (4π·σ·cosθ/λ)²; with σ = 0.1 nm at normal incidence and λ = 13.5 nm, TIS ≈ (4π×0.1/13.5)² ≈ 0.0087, about 0.9% of the light, and about 3.5% for σ = 0.2 nm.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「面形誤差、中高頻粗糙度與散射」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Figure error, mid/high-spatial-frequency roughness and scatter\", which statement holds?","options":["λ/4 的面形品質對任何波長都是「繞射極限」。","總積分散射近似為 TIS ≈ (4π·σ·cosθ/λ)²。","每片鏡子都通過驗收，整組光學就自動合格。"],"optionsEn":["λ/4 figure quality is diffraction limited at any wavelength.","Total integrated scatter is approximately TIS ≈ (4π·σ·cosθ/λ)².","If every mirror passes, the assembled optics automatically pass."],"answer":1,"explanation":"總積分散射近似為 TIS ≈ (4π·σ·cosθ/λ)²；取 σ = 0.1 nm、正向入射、λ = 13.5 nm，TIS ≈ (4π×0.1/13.5)² ≈ 0.0087，即約 0.9% 的光被散射；σ = 0.2 nm 時約 3.5%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Total integrated scatter is approximately TIS ≈ (4π·σ·cosθ/λ)²; with σ = 0.1 nm at normal incidence and λ = 13.5 nm, TIS ≈ (4π×0.1/13.5)² ≈ 0.0087, about 0.9% of the light, and about 3.5% for σ = 0.2 nm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"a402-v12-11","title":"面形誤差、中高頻粗糙度與散射：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Figure error, mid/high-spatial-frequency roughness and scatter: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「基板面形與粗糙度頻譜」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Substrate figure and roughness spectrum” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"以干涉儀量面形、以白光干涉或 AFM 量不同取樣長度的粗糙度，將功率譜密度（PSD）依頻段積分成三個 σ 值，再用 TIS 公式估散射損失並與反射率量測差額比對。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure figure with an interferometer and roughness at several sampling lengths with white-light interferometry or AFM, integrate the power spectral density into three band-limited σ values, then estimate scatter loss with the TIS relation and compare with the reflectance shortfall. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：拋光若只追求低頻面形而留下週期數十微米的中頻波紋，成像會出現對比下降的眩光，即使面形與反射率各自合格。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Polishing that chases low-frequency figure while leaving tens-of-micrometre mid-frequency ripple produces contrast-robbing flare even when figure and reflectance each pass.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以干涉儀量面形、以白光干涉或 AFM 量不同取樣長度的粗糙度，將功率譜密度（PSD）依頻段積分成三個 σ 值，再用 TIS 公式估散射損失並與反射率量測差額比對。","textEn":"Measure figure with an interferometer and roughness at several sampling lengths with white-light interferometry or AFM, integrate the power spectral density into three band-limited σ values, then estimate scatter loss with the TIS relation and compare with the reflectance shortfall.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-11-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「面形誤差、中高頻粗糙度與散射」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Figure error, mid/high-spatial-frequency roughness and scatter\"?","options":["只看單次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準件或重複量測。","只要材料夠純、夠透明，EUV 也能像 DUV 一樣用透鏡成像。","以干涉儀量面形、以白光干涉或 AFM 量不同取樣長度的粗糙度，將功率譜密度（PSD）依頻段積分成三個 σ 值，再用 TIS 公式估散射損失並與反射率量測差額比對。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the result; no reference artefact or repeat measurement is needed.","With pure enough transparent material, EUV could be imaged with lenses like DUV.","Measure figure with an interferometer and roughness at several sampling lengths with white-light interferometry or AFM, integrate the power spectral density into three band-limited σ values, then estimate scatter loss with the TIS relation and compare with the reflectance shortfall."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以干涉儀量面形、以白光干涉或 AFM 量不同取樣長度的粗糙度，將功率譜密度（PSD）依頻段積分成三個 σ 值，再用 TIS 公式估散射損失並與反射率量測差額比對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure figure with an interferometer and roughness at several sampling lengths with white-light interferometry or AFM, integrate the power spectral density into three band-limited σ values, then estimate scatter loss with the TIS relation and compare with the reflectance shortfall. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"a402-v12-12","title":"面形誤差、中高頻粗糙度與散射：失效診斷","titleEn":"Figure error, mid/high-spatial-frequency roughness and scatter: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「基板面形與粗糙度頻譜」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Substrate figure and roughness spectrum” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"拋光若只追求低頻面形而留下週期數十微米的中頻波紋，成像會出現對比下降的眩光，即使面形與反射率各自合格。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Polishing that chases low-frequency figure while leaving tens-of-micrometre mid-frequency ripple produces contrast-robbing flare even when figure and reflectance each pass. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：因為波長只有 13.5 nm，可接受的粗糙度是 0.1 nm 等級，比可見光光學嚴格兩個數量級。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Because the wavelength is only 13.5 nm, acceptable roughness is of order 0.1 nm, two orders of magnitude tighter than visible optics.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「達到可見光光學的光滑度，對 EUV 也足夠。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A surface smooth enough for visible optics is smooth enough for EUV.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"拋光若只追求低頻面形而留下週期數十微米的中頻波紋，成像會出現對比下降的眩光，即使面形與反射率各自合格。","textEn":"Polishing that chases low-frequency figure while leaving tens-of-micrometre mid-frequency ripple produces contrast-robbing flare even when figure and reflectance each pass.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「面形誤差、中高頻粗糙度與散射」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Figure error, mid/high-spatial-frequency roughness and scatter\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["拋光若只追求低頻面形而留下週期數十微米的中頻波紋，成像會出現對比下降的眩光，即使面形與反射率各自合格。","異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","基板很厚時，幾百奈米薄膜的應力可以忽略。"],"optionsEn":["Polishing that chases low-frequency figure while leaving tens-of-micrometre mid-frequency ripple produces contrast-robbing flare even when figure and reflectance each pass.","An anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","For a thick substrate the stress of a few hundred nanometres of film is negligible."],"answer":0,"explanation":"拋光若只追求低頻面形而留下週期數十微米的中頻波紋，成像會出現對比下降的眩光，即使面形與反射率各自合格。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Polishing that chases low-frequency figure while leaving tens-of-micrometre mid-frequency ripple produces contrast-robbing flare even when figure and reflectance each pass. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"a402-v12-13","title":"鍍膜製程與多層膜應力：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Deposition process and multilayer stress: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-12"],"objective":"說明「濺鍍腔與膜應力」如何決定EUV 多層膜反射鏡的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sputter chamber and coating stress” determines the key performance of “EUV multilayer mirrors”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"多層膜通常以磁控濺鍍或離子束濺鍍逐層沉積，並以石英晶體或原位反射率監控厚度；每層厚度誤差必須控制在 0.01 nm 等級。Mo/Si 多層膜通常帶有數百 MPa 的壓應力，會把基板彎曲並改變已拋光好的面形，因此需要應力補償層、退火或在設計階段預留變形量。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「濺鍍腔與膜應力」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Multilayers are deposited layer by layer by magnetron or ion-beam sputtering with quartz-crystal or in-situ reflectance thickness control; per-layer errors must stay near 0.01 nm. Mo/Si stacks typically carry several hundred MPa of compressive stress that bends the substrate and alters the polished figure, so compensation layers, annealing or pre-compensated figure are required. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Sputter chamber and coating stress”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：Stoney 關係給出鍍膜後的曲率 κ = 6σ_f·t_f·(1 − ν_s)/(E_s·t_s²)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Stoney's relation gives the post-coating curvature κ = 6σ_f·t_f·(1 − ν_s)/(E_s·t_s²).","failure":"常見誤解：「基板很厚時，幾百奈米薄膜的應力可以忽略。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"For a thick substrate the stress of a few hundred nanometres of film is negligible.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「濺鍍腔與膜應力」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Sputter chamber and coating stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-13-k1","title":"鍍膜製程與多層膜應力","titleEn":"Deposition process and multilayer stress","text":"多層膜通常以磁控濺鍍或離子束濺鍍逐層沉積，並以石英晶體或原位反射率監控厚度；每層厚度誤差必須控制在 0.01 nm 等級。Mo/Si 多層膜通常帶有數百 MPa 的壓應力，會把基板彎曲並改變已拋光好的面形，因此需要應力補償層、退火或在設計階段預留變形量。","textEn":"Multilayers are deposited layer by layer by magnetron or ion-beam sputtering with quartz-crystal or in-situ reflectance thickness control; per-layer errors must stay near 0.01 nm. Mo/Si stacks typically carry several hundred MPa of compressive stress that bends the substrate and alters the polished figure, so compensation layers, annealing or pre-compensated figure are required.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：基板很厚時，幾百奈米薄膜的應力可以忽略。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: For a thick substrate the stress of a few hundred nanometres of film is negligible. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鍍膜製程與多層膜應力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Deposition process and multilayer stress\" is correct?","options":["基板很厚時，幾百奈米薄膜的應力可以忽略。","多層膜通常以磁控濺鍍或離子束濺鍍逐層沉積，並以石英晶體或原位反射率監控厚度；每層厚度誤差必須控制在 0.01 nm 等級。","在真空中工作的鏡面不會受到污染。"],"optionsEn":["For a thick substrate the stress of a few hundred nanometres of film is negligible.","Multilayers are deposited layer by layer by magnetron or ion-beam sputtering with quartz-crystal or in-situ reflectance thickness control.","A mirror working in vacuum cannot get contaminated."],"answer":1,"explanation":"多層膜通常以磁控濺鍍或離子束濺鍍逐層沉積，並以石英晶體或原位反射率監控厚度；每層厚度誤差必須控制在 0.01 nm 等級。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Multilayers are deposited layer by layer by magnetron or ion-beam sputtering with quartz-crystal or in-situ reflectance thickness control; per-layer errors must stay near 0.01 nm. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"a402-v12-14","title":"鍍膜製程與多層膜應力：定量估算","titleEn":"Deposition process and multilayer stress: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「濺鍍腔與膜應力」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sputter chamber and coating stress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：Stoney 關係給出鍍膜後的曲率 κ = 6σ_f·t_f·(1 − ν_s)/(E_s·t_s²)。取膜應力 σ_f = −400 MPa、總膜厚 t_f = 350 nm、ULE 基板 E_s = 67.6 GPa、ν_s = 0.17、厚度 t_s = 50 mm，κ ≈ 6×400e6×350e−9×0.83/(67.6e9×0.0025) ≈ 4.1×10⁻⁶ m⁻¹；對半徑 100 mm 的鏡面，矢高變化 ≈ κr²/2 ≈ 21 nm，遠超過次奈米面形預算。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Stoney's relation gives the post-coating curvature κ = 6σ_f·t_f·(1 − ν_s)/(E_s·t_s²). With σ_f = −400 MPa, total film thickness t_f = 350 nm, a ULE substrate with E_s = 67.6 GPa, ν_s = 0.17 and t_s = 50 mm, κ ≈ 6×400e6×350e−9×0.83/(67.6e9×0.0025) ≈ 4.1×10⁻⁶ m⁻¹; over a 100 mm radius the sag change is ≈ κr²/2 ≈ 21 nm, far beyond a sub-nanometre figure budget. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：鍍膜前後各量一次面形並相減，與 Stoney 預測的球面項比較；若殘差含非球面項，表示應力沿鏡面不均勻或夾持造成變形，需另外分析。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure figure before and after coating and subtract; compare the difference with the Stoney spherical term.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"Stoney 關係給出鍍膜後的曲率 κ = 6σ_f·t_f·(1 − ν_s)/(E_s·t_s²)。取膜應力 σ_f = −400 MPa、總膜厚 t_f = 350 nm、ULE 基板 E_s = 67.6 GPa、ν_s = 0.17、厚度 t_s = 50 mm，κ ≈ 6×400e6×350e−9×0.83/(67.6e9×0.0025) ≈ 4.1×10⁻⁶ m⁻¹；對半徑 100 mm 的鏡面，矢高變化 ≈ κr²/2 ≈ 21 nm，遠超過次奈米面形預算。","textEn":"Stoney's relation gives the post-coating curvature κ = 6σ_f·t_f·(1 − ν_s)/(E_s·t_s²). With σ_f = −400 MPa, total film thickness t_f = 350 nm, a ULE substrate with E_s = 67.6 GPa, ν_s = 0.17 and t_s = 50 mm, κ ≈ 6×400e6×350e−9×0.83/(67.6e9×0.0025) ≈ 4.1×10⁻⁶ m⁻¹; over a 100 mm radius the sag change is ≈ κr²/2 ≈ 21 nm, far beyond a sub-nanometre figure budget.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鍍膜製程與多層膜應力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Deposition process and multilayer stress\", which statement holds?","options":["超低膨脹材料就表示熱變形為零。","只要材料夠純、夠透明，EUV 也能像 DUV 一樣用透鏡成像。","Stoney 關係給出鍍膜後的曲率 κ = 6σ_f·t_f·(1 − ν_s)/(E_s·t_s²)。"],"optionsEn":["Ultralow-expansion material means zero thermal deformation.","With pure enough transparent material, EUV could be imaged with lenses like DUV.","Stoney's relation gives the post-coating curvature κ = 6σ_f·t_f·(1 − ν_s)/(E_s·t_s²)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Stoney 關係給出鍍膜後的曲率 κ = 6σ_f·t_f·(1 − ν_s)/(E_s·t_s²)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Stoney's relation gives the post-coating curvature κ = 6σ_f·t_f·(1 − ν_s)/(E_s·t_s²). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"a402-v12-15","title":"鍍膜製程與多層膜應力：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Deposition process and multilayer stress: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「濺鍍腔與膜應力」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Sputter chamber and coating stress” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"鍍膜前後各量一次面形並相減，與 Stoney 預測的球面項比較；若殘差含非球面項，表示應力沿鏡面不均勻或夾持造成變形，需另外分析。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure figure before and after coating and subtract; compare the difference with the Stoney spherical term. Residual non-spherical terms indicate stress non-uniformity or mounting-induced deformation that needs separate analysis. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：忽略應力的鏡面在鍍膜後面形超差，只能重新修形並重鍍；若重鍍時週期控制又偏移，反射率與面形兩項同時不合格。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: A mirror coated without stress accounting fails figure after coating and must be refigured and recoated; if period control drifts on the recoat, both reflectance and figure fail together.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"鍍膜前後各量一次面形並相減，與 Stoney 預測的球面項比較；若殘差含非球面項，表示應力沿鏡面不均勻或夾持造成變形，需另外分析。","textEn":"Measure figure before and after coating and subtract; compare the difference with the Stoney spherical term. Residual non-spherical terms indicate stress non-uniformity or mounting-induced deformation that needs separate analysis.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-15-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鍍膜製程與多層膜應力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Deposition process and multilayer stress\"?","options":["鍍膜前後各量一次面形並相減，與 Stoney 預測的球面項比較；若殘差含非球面項，表示應力沿鏡面不均勻或夾持造成變形，需另外分析。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","雙層數越多，反射率一定越高。"],"optionsEn":["Measure figure before and after coating and subtract; compare the difference with the Stoney spherical term.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","More bilayers always give higher reflectance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"鍍膜前後各量一次面形並相減，與 Stoney 預測的球面項比較；若殘差含非球面項，表示應力沿鏡面不均勻或夾持造成變形，需另外分析。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure figure before and after coating and subtract; compare the difference with the Stoney spherical term. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"a402-v12-16","title":"鍍膜製程與多層膜應力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Deposition process and multilayer stress: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「濺鍍腔與膜應力」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Sputter chamber and coating stress” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"忽略應力的鏡面在鍍膜後面形超差，只能重新修形並重鍍；若重鍍時週期控制又偏移，反射率與面形兩項同時不合格。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"A mirror coated without stress accounting fails figure after coating and must be refigured and recoated; if period control drifts on the recoat, both reflectance and figure fail together. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：Mo/Si 多層膜通常帶有數百 MPa 的壓應力，會把基板彎曲並改變已拋光好的面形，因此需要應力補償層、退火或在設計階段預留變形量。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Mo/Si stacks typically carry several hundred MPa of compressive stress that bends the substrate and alters the polished figure, so compensation layers, annealing or pre-compensated figure are required.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「基板很厚時，幾百奈米薄膜的應力可以忽略。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"For a thick substrate the stress of a few hundred nanometres of film is negligible.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略應力的鏡面在鍍膜後面形超差，只能重新修形並重鍍；若重鍍時週期控制又偏移，反射率與面形兩項同時不合格。","textEn":"A mirror coated without stress accounting fails figure after coating and must be refigured and recoated; if period control drifts on the recoat, both reflectance and figure fail together.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鍍膜製程與多層膜應力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Deposition process and multilayer stress\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的零件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","忽略應力的鏡面在鍍膜後面形超差，只能重新修形並重鍍；若重鍍時週期控制又偏移，反射率與面形兩項同時不合格。","在真空中工作的鏡面不會受到污染。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive part first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A mirror coated without stress accounting fails figure after coating and must be refigured and recoated.","A mirror working in vacuum cannot get contaminated."],"answer":1,"explanation":"忽略應力的鏡面在鍍膜後面形超差，只能重新修形並重鍍；若重鍍時週期控制又偏移，反射率與面形兩項同時不合格。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A mirror coated without stress accounting fails figure after coating and must be refigured and recoated; if period control drifts on the recoat, both reflectance and figure fail together. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"a402-v12-s3","title":"量測、校正與誤差預算","titleEn":"Measurement, calibration and error budgets","description":"本階段聚焦「表面污染、氧化與覆蓋層」與「波前誤差預算與 Strehl 判準」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Surface contamination, oxidation and capping layers\" and \"Wavefront-error budget and the Strehl criterion\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a402-v12-17","title":"表面污染、氧化與覆蓋層：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Surface contamination, oxidation and capping layers: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-16"],"objective":"說明「Ru 覆蓋層與氫清潔」如何決定EUV 多層膜反射鏡的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ruthenium capping layer and hydrogen cleaning” determines the key performance of “EUV multilayer mirrors”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"EUV 光子與殘留碳氫化合物作用會在鏡面沉積碳；殘留水氣則使最上層 Si 氧化，氧化通常不可逆。因此多層膜頂部加上數奈米的 Ru 覆蓋層抗氧化，並以氫自由基清潔週期性移除碳膜。真空腔的殘氣分壓、材料除氣與光罩附近的清潔策略都屬於鏡面壽命工程。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「Ru 覆蓋層與氫清潔」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"EUV photons react with residual hydrocarbons to deposit carbon on the mirror, while residual water oxidises the top silicon layer, usually irreversibly. A few nanometres of ruthenium capping resists oxidation, and hydrogen-radical cleaning periodically removes carbon films. Residual-gas partial pressures, material outgassing and cleaning strategy near the reticle are all part of mirror-lifetime engineering. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Ruthenium capping layer and hydrogen cleaning”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：厚度 t_C 的碳膜使反射率近似按 R ≈ R₀·exp(−2·α_C·t_C) 衰減，其中 α_C = 4πβ/λ 為碳在 13.5 nm 的吸收係數（β ≈ 0.007 時約 0.0065 nm⁻¹）；t_C = 1 nm 時反射率約損失 1.3%，六片鏡子各長 1 nm 碳就損失約 7.5% 通量。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A carbon film of thickness t_C reduces reflectance roughly as R ≈ R₀·exp(−2·α_C·t_C) with α_C = 4πβ/λ the carbon absorption coefficient at 13.5 nm (about 0.0065 nm⁻¹ for β ≈ 0.007); t_C = 1 nm costs about 1.3% reflectance, and 1 nm of carbon on each of six mirrors loses about 7.5% throughput.","failure":"常見誤解：「在真空中工作的鏡面不會受到污染。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A mirror working in vacuum cannot get contaminated.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「Ru 覆蓋層與氫清潔」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Ruthenium capping layer and hydrogen cleaning”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-17-k1","title":"表面污染、氧化與覆蓋層","titleEn":"Surface contamination, oxidation and capping layers","text":"EUV 光子與殘留碳氫化合物作用會在鏡面沉積碳；殘留水氣則使最上層 Si 氧化，氧化通常不可逆。因此多層膜頂部加上數奈米的 Ru 覆蓋層抗氧化，並以氫自由基清潔週期性移除碳膜。","textEn":"EUV photons react with residual hydrocarbons to deposit carbon on the mirror, while residual water oxidises the top silicon layer, usually irreversibly. A few nanometres of ruthenium capping resists oxidation, and hydrogen-radical cleaning periodically removes carbon films.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：在真空中工作的鏡面不會受到污染。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A mirror working in vacuum cannot get contaminated. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「表面污染、氧化與覆蓋層」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Surface contamination, oxidation and capping layers\" is correct?","options":["在真空中工作的鏡面不會受到污染。","λ/4 的面形品質對任何波長都是「繞射極限」。","EUV 光子與殘留碳氫化合物作用會在鏡面沉積碳；殘留水氣則使最上層 Si 氧化，氧化通常不可逆。"],"optionsEn":["A mirror working in vacuum cannot get contaminated.","λ/4 figure quality is diffraction limited at any wavelength.","EUV photons react with residual hydrocarbons to deposit carbon on the mirror, while residual water oxidises the top silicon layer, usually irreversibly."],"answer":2,"explanation":"EUV 光子與殘留碳氫化合物作用會在鏡面沉積碳；殘留水氣則使最上層 Si 氧化，氧化通常不可逆。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"EUV photons react with residual hydrocarbons to deposit carbon on the mirror, while residual water oxidises the top silicon layer, usually irreversibly. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"a402-v12-18","title":"表面污染、氧化與覆蓋層：定量估算","titleEn":"Surface contamination, oxidation and capping layers: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「Ru 覆蓋層與氫清潔」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ruthenium capping layer and hydrogen cleaning” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：厚度 t_C 的碳膜使反射率近似按 R ≈ R₀·exp(−2·α_C·t_C) 衰減，其中 α_C = 4πβ/λ 為碳在 13.5 nm 的吸收係數（β ≈ 0.007 時約 0.0065 nm⁻¹）；t_C = 1 nm 時反射率約損失 1.3%，六片鏡子各長 1 nm 碳就損失約 7.5% 通量。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A carbon film of thickness t_C reduces reflectance roughly as R ≈ R₀·exp(−2·α_C·t_C) with α_C = 4πβ/λ the carbon absorption coefficient at 13.5 nm (about 0.0065 nm⁻¹ for β ≈ 0.007); t_C = 1 nm costs about 1.3% reflectance, and 1 nm of carbon on each of six mirrors loses about 7.5% throughput. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：以原位或定期的反射率監測追蹤衰減速率，用 XPS 或橢偏儀估碳膜厚度與覆蓋層氧化狀態，並確認氫清潔後反射率是否回到基準。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Track the decay rate with in-situ or periodic reflectance monitoring, estimate carbon thickness and cap oxidation by XPS or ellipsometry, and confirm that reflectance returns to baseline after hydrogen cleaning.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"厚度 t_C 的碳膜使反射率近似按 R ≈ R₀·exp(−2·α_C·t_C) 衰減，其中 α_C = 4πβ/λ 為碳在 13.5 nm 的吸收係數（β ≈ 0.007 時約 0.0065 nm⁻¹）；t_C = 1 nm 時反射率約損失 1.3%，六片鏡子各長 1 nm 碳就損失約 7.5% 通量。","textEn":"A carbon film of thickness t_C reduces reflectance roughly as R ≈ R₀·exp(−2·α_C·t_C) with α_C = 4πβ/λ the carbon absorption coefficient at 13.5 nm (about 0.0065 nm⁻¹ for β ≈ 0.007); t_C = 1 nm costs about 1.3% reflectance, and 1 nm of carbon on each of six mirrors loses about 7.5% throughput.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「表面污染、氧化與覆蓋層」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Surface contamination, oxidation and capping layers\", which statement holds?","options":["厚度 t_C 的碳膜使反射率近似按 R ≈ R₀·exp(−2·α_C·t_C) 衰減，其中 α_C = 4πβ/λ 為碳在 13.5 nm 的吸收係數（β ≈ 0.007 時約 0.0065 nm⁻¹）。","每片鏡子都通過驗收，整組光學就自動合格。","雙層數越多，反射率一定越高。"],"optionsEn":["A carbon film of thickness t_C reduces reflectance roughly as R ≈ R₀·exp(−2·α_C·t_C) with α_C = 4πβ/λ the carbon absorption coefficient at 13.5 nm (about 0.0065 nm⁻¹ for β ≈ 0.007).","If every mirror passes, the assembled optics automatically pass.","More bilayers always give higher reflectance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"厚度 t_C 的碳膜使反射率近似按 R ≈ R₀·exp(−2·α_C·t_C) 衰減，其中 α_C = 4πβ/λ 為碳在 13.5 nm 的吸收係數（β ≈ 0.007 時約 0.0065 nm⁻¹）；t_C = 1 nm 時反射率約損失 1.3%，六片鏡子各長 1 nm 碳就損失約 7.5% 通量。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A carbon film of thickness t_C reduces reflectance roughly as R ≈ R₀·exp(−2·α_C·t_C) with α_C = 4πβ/λ the carbon absorption coefficient at 13.5 nm (about 0.0065 nm⁻¹ for β ≈ 0.007); t_C = 1 nm costs about 1.3% reflectance, and 1 nm of carbon on each of six mirrors loses about 7.5% throughput. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"a402-v12-19","title":"表面污染、氧化與覆蓋層：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Surface contamination, oxidation and capping layers: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「Ru 覆蓋層與氫清潔」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Ruthenium capping layer and hydrogen cleaning” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"以原位或定期的反射率監測追蹤衰減速率，用 XPS 或橢偏儀估碳膜厚度與覆蓋層氧化狀態，並確認氫清潔後反射率是否回到基準。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Track the decay rate with in-situ or periodic reflectance monitoring, estimate carbon thickness and cap oxidation by XPS or ellipsometry, and confirm that reflectance returns to baseline after hydrogen cleaning. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：若把 Si 當最外層，水氣氧化使反射率永久下降；若氫清潔過強，會侵蝕或起泡覆蓋層，同樣造成不可逆損失。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Leaving silicon as the outermost layer lets water oxidation permanently lower reflectance; over-aggressive hydrogen cleaning erodes or blisters the cap, also irreversibly.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以原位或定期的反射率監測追蹤衰減速率，用 XPS 或橢偏儀估碳膜厚度與覆蓋層氧化狀態，並確認氫清潔後反射率是否回到基準。","textEn":"Track the decay rate with in-situ or periodic reflectance monitoring, estimate carbon thickness and cap oxidation by XPS or ellipsometry, and confirm that reflectance returns to baseline after hydrogen cleaning.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-19-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「表面污染、氧化與覆蓋層」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Surface contamination, oxidation and capping layers\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","以原位或定期的反射率監測追蹤衰減速率，用 XPS 或橢偏儀估碳膜厚度與覆蓋層氧化狀態，並確認氫清潔後反射率是否回到基準。","達到可見光光學的光滑度，對 EUV 也足夠。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Track the decay rate with in-situ or periodic reflectance monitoring, estimate carbon thickness and cap oxidation by XPS or ellipsometry, and confirm that reflectance returns to baseline after hydrogen cleaning.","A surface smooth enough for visible optics is smooth enough for EUV."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以原位或定期的反射率監測追蹤衰減速率，用 XPS 或橢偏儀估碳膜厚度與覆蓋層氧化狀態，並確認氫清潔後反射率是否回到基準。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Track the decay rate with in-situ or periodic reflectance monitoring, estimate carbon thickness and cap oxidation by XPS or ellipsometry, and confirm that reflectance returns to baseline after hydrogen cleaning. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"a402-v12-20","title":"表面污染、氧化與覆蓋層：失效診斷","titleEn":"Surface contamination, oxidation and capping layers: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「Ru 覆蓋層與氫清潔」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Ruthenium capping layer and hydrogen cleaning” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"若把 Si 當最外層，水氣氧化使反射率永久下降；若氫清潔過強，會侵蝕或起泡覆蓋層，同樣造成不可逆損失。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Leaving silicon as the outermost layer lets water oxidation permanently lower reflectance; over-aggressive hydrogen cleaning erodes or blisters the cap, also irreversibly. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：真空腔的殘氣分壓、材料除氣與光罩附近的清潔策略都屬於鏡面壽命工程。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Residual-gas partial pressures, material outgassing and cleaning strategy near the reticle are all part of mirror-lifetime engineering.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「在真空中工作的鏡面不會受到污染。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A mirror working in vacuum cannot get contaminated.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若把 Si 當最外層，水氣氧化使反射率永久下降；若氫清潔過強，會侵蝕或起泡覆蓋層，同樣造成不可逆損失。","textEn":"Leaving silicon as the outermost layer lets water oxidation permanently lower reflectance; over-aggressive hydrogen cleaning erodes or blisters the cap, also irreversibly.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「表面污染、氧化與覆蓋層」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Surface contamination, oxidation and capping layers\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","λ/4 的面形品質對任何波長都是「繞射極限」。","若把 Si 當最外層，水氣氧化使反射率永久下降；若氫清潔過強，會侵蝕或起泡覆蓋層，同樣造成不可逆損失。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","λ/4 figure quality is diffraction limited at any wavelength.","Leaving silicon as the outermost layer lets water oxidation permanently lower reflectance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若把 Si 當最外層，水氣氧化使反射率永久下降；若氫清潔過強，會侵蝕或起泡覆蓋層，同樣造成不可逆損失。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Leaving silicon as the outermost layer lets water oxidation permanently lower reflectance; over-aggressive hydrogen cleaning erodes or blisters the cap, also irreversibly. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"a402-v12-21","title":"波前誤差預算與 Strehl 判準：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Wavefront-error budget and the Strehl criterion: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-20"],"objective":"說明「波前誤差預算表」如何決定EUV 多層膜反射鏡的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Wavefront-error budget table” determines the key performance of “EUV multilayer mirrors”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"投影光學由多片反射鏡組成，每片面形誤差在反射時加倍計入波前。影像品質以 RMS 波前誤差衡量，Maréchal 判準要求總 RMS 約小於 λ/14 才能維持 Strehl 比 0.8；在 13.5 nm 這相當於約 1 nm。各鏡的面形、鍍膜、對準與熱變形必須以均方根相加分配到次奈米等級。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「波前誤差預算表」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Projection optics use several mirrors, and each mirror's figure error enters the wavefront twice on reflection. Image quality is judged by RMS wavefront error; the Maréchal criterion asks for a total RMS below about λ/14 to keep a Strehl ratio of 0.8, which at 13.5 nm is about 1 nm. Figure, coating, alignment and thermal terms of every mirror must be allocated root-sum-square to sub-nanometre values. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Wavefront-error budget table”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：Strehl ≈ exp[−(2πσ/λ)²]。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Strehl ≈ exp[−(2πσ/λ)²].","failure":"常見誤解：「λ/4 的面形品質對任何波長都是「繞射極限」。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"λ/4 figure quality is diffraction limited at any wavelength.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「波前誤差預算表」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Wavefront-error budget table”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-21-k1","title":"波前誤差預算與 Strehl 判準","titleEn":"Wavefront-error budget and the Strehl criterion","text":"投影光學由多片反射鏡組成，每片面形誤差在反射時加倍計入波前。影像品質以 RMS 波前誤差衡量，Maréchal 判準要求總 RMS 約小於 λ/14 才能維持 Strehl 比 0.8；在 13.5 nm 這相當於約 1 nm。","textEn":"Projection optics use several mirrors, and each mirror's figure error enters the wavefront twice on reflection. Image quality is judged by RMS wavefront error; the Maréchal criterion asks for a total RMS below about λ/14 to keep a Strehl ratio of 0.8, which at 13.5 nm is about 1 nm.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：λ/4 的面形品質對任何波長都是「繞射極限」。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: λ/4 figure quality is diffraction limited at any wavelength. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「波前誤差預算與 Strehl 判準」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Wavefront-error budget and the Strehl criterion\" is correct?","options":["投影光學由多片反射鏡組成，每片面形誤差在反射時加倍計入波前。","λ/4 的面形品質對任何波長都是「繞射極限」。","超低膨脹材料就表示熱變形為零。"],"optionsEn":["Projection optics use several mirrors, and each mirror's figure error enters the wavefront twice on reflection.","λ/4 figure quality is diffraction limited at any wavelength.","Ultralow-expansion material means zero thermal deformation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"投影光學由多片反射鏡組成，每片面形誤差在反射時加倍計入波前。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Projection optics use several mirrors, and each mirror's figure error enters the wavefront twice on reflection. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"a402-v12-22","title":"波前誤差預算與 Strehl 判準：定量估算","titleEn":"Wavefront-error budget and the Strehl criterion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「波前誤差預算表」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Wavefront-error budget table” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：Strehl ≈ exp[−(2πσ/λ)²]。σ = 1.0 nm 時，(2π×1/13.5)² = 0.217，Strehl ≈ 0.805；σ = 1.5 nm 時約 0.614。六片鏡子若各分配 σᵢ，總和為 σ_total = √(Σσᵢ²)，且每片的面形貢獻 ≈ 2·figure_RMS·cosθ。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Strehl ≈ exp[−(2πσ/λ)²]. For σ = 1.0 nm, (2π×1/13.5)² = 0.217 and Strehl ≈ 0.805; for σ = 1.5 nm it is about 0.614. With six mirrors allocated σᵢ each, σ_total = √(Σσᵢ²), and each mirror's figure contribution is ≈ 2·figure_RMS·cosθ. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：建立預算表：列出每片鏡子的面形、鍍膜、對準、熱與量測不確定度，計算 RSS 並與允收值比較；再用波長相同的干涉量測或系統波前量測反推 Zernike 項，核對哪一項吃掉最多預算。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build the budget table listing figure, coating, alignment, thermal and metrology uncertainty per mirror, compute the RSS and compare with the allowance; then use at-wavelength or system wavefront measurement to back out Zernike terms and see which item consumes the most budget.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"Strehl ≈ exp[−(2πσ/λ)²]。σ = 1.0 nm 時，(2π×1/13.5)² = 0.217，Strehl ≈ 0.805；σ = 1.5 nm 時約 0.614。六片鏡子若各分配 σᵢ，總和為 σ_total = √(Σσᵢ²)，且每片的面形貢獻 ≈ 2·figure_RMS·cosθ。","textEn":"Strehl ≈ exp[−(2πσ/λ)²]. For σ = 1.0 nm, (2π×1/13.5)² = 0.217 and Strehl ≈ 0.805; for σ = 1.5 nm it is about 0.614. With six mirrors allocated σᵢ each, σ_total = √(Σσᵢ²), and each mirror's figure contribution is ≈ 2·figure_RMS·cosθ.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「波前誤差預算與 Strehl 判準」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Wavefront-error budget and the Strehl criterion\", which statement holds?","options":["只要材料夠純、夠透明，EUV 也能像 DUV 一樣用透鏡成像。","Strehl ≈ exp[−(2πσ/λ)²]。","達到可見光光學的光滑度，對 EUV 也足夠。"],"optionsEn":["With pure enough transparent material, EUV could be imaged with lenses like DUV.","Strehl ≈ exp[−(2πσ/λ)²].","A surface smooth enough for visible optics is smooth enough for EUV."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Strehl ≈ exp[−(2πσ/λ)²]。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Strehl ≈ exp[−(2πσ/λ)²]. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"a402-v12-23","title":"波前誤差預算與 Strehl 判準：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Wavefront-error budget and the Strehl criterion: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「波前誤差預算表」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Wavefront-error budget table” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"建立預算表：列出每片鏡子的面形、鍍膜、對準、熱與量測不確定度，計算 RSS 並與允收值比較；再用波長相同的干涉量測或系統波前量測反推 Zernike 項，核對哪一項吃掉最多預算。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build the budget table listing figure, coating, alignment, thermal and metrology uncertainty per mirror, compute the RSS and compare with the allowance; then use at-wavelength or system wavefront measurement to back out Zernike terms and see which item consumes the most budget. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：把 PV（峰谷）與 RMS 混用、或把同一來源重複計入兩個項目，會讓預算表看似合格但實際影像對比不足。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Mixing peak-to-valley with RMS values, or double-counting one source under two items, makes the budget look compliant while the real image contrast falls short.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"建立預算表：列出每片鏡子的面形、鍍膜、對準、熱與量測不確定度，計算 RSS 並與允收值比較；再用波長相同的干涉量測或系統波前量測反推 Zernike 項，核對哪一項吃掉最多預算。","textEn":"Build the budget table listing figure, coating, alignment, thermal and metrology uncertainty per mirror, compute the RSS and compare with the allowance; then use at-wavelength or system wavefront measurement to back out Zernike terms and see which item consumes the most budget.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-23-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「波前誤差預算與 Strehl 判準」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Wavefront-error budget and the Strehl criterion\"?","options":["只要模擬結果看起來合理，就可以省略實體量測與校正。","基板很厚時，幾百奈米薄膜的應力可以忽略。","建立預算表：列出每片鏡子的面形、鍍膜、對準、熱與量測不確定度，計算 RSS 並與允收值比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the simulation looks reasonable, physical measurement and calibration can be skipped.","For a thick substrate the stress of a few hundred nanometres of film is negligible.","Build the budget table listing figure, coating, alignment, thermal and metrology uncertainty per mirror, compute the RSS and compare with the allowance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"建立預算表：列出每片鏡子的面形、鍍膜、對準、熱與量測不確定度，計算 RSS 並與允收值比較；再用波長相同的干涉量測或系統波前量測反推 Zernike 項，核對哪一項吃掉最多預算。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build the budget table listing figure, coating, alignment, thermal and metrology uncertainty per mirror, compute the RSS and compare with the allowance; then use at-wavelength or system wavefront measurement to back out Zernike terms and see which item consumes the most budget. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"a402-v12-24","title":"波前誤差預算與 Strehl 判準：失效診斷","titleEn":"Wavefront-error budget and the Strehl criterion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「波前誤差預算表」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Wavefront-error budget table” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"把 PV（峰谷）與 RMS 混用、或把同一來源重複計入兩個項目，會讓預算表看似合格但實際影像對比不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Mixing peak-to-valley with RMS values, or double-counting one source under two items, makes the budget look compliant while the real image contrast falls short. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：各鏡的面形、鍍膜、對準與熱變形必須以均方根相加分配到次奈米等級。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Figure, coating, alignment and thermal terms of every mirror must be allocated root-sum-square to sub-nanometre values.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「λ/4 的面形品質對任何波長都是「繞射極限」。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"λ/4 figure quality is diffraction limited at any wavelength.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把 PV（峰谷）與 RMS 混用、或把同一來源重複計入兩個項目，會讓預算表看似合格但實際影像對比不足。","textEn":"Mixing peak-to-valley with RMS values, or double-counting one source under two items, makes the budget look compliant while the real image contrast falls short.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「波前誤差預算與 Strehl 判準」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Wavefront-error budget and the Strehl criterion\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把 PV（峰谷）與 RMS 混用、或把同一來源重複計入兩個項目，會讓預算表看似合格但實際影像對比不足。","只要重新開機或重設軟體，硬體失效也會一併排除。","超低膨脹材料就表示熱變形為零。"],"optionsEn":["Mixing peak-to-valley with RMS values, or double-counting one source under two items, makes the budget look compliant while the real image contrast falls short.","Restarting or resetting the software also clears hardware failures.","Ultralow-expansion material means zero thermal deformation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把 PV（峰谷）與 RMS 混用、或把同一來源重複計入兩個項目，會讓預算表看似合格但實際影像對比不足。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mixing peak-to-valley with RMS values, or double-counting one source under two items, makes the budget look compliant while the real image contrast falls short. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"a402-v12-s4","title":"系統整合、驗證與工程交接","titleEn":"Integration, validation and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「熱負載、低膨脹材料與面形漂移」與「鏡組整合、對準與驗收」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Thermal load, ultralow-expansion materials and figure drift\" and \"Mirror-set integration, alignment and acceptance\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a402-v12-25","title":"熱負載、低膨脹材料與面形漂移：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Thermal load, ultralow-expansion materials and figure drift: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-24"],"objective":"說明「熱控與低膨脹基板」如何決定EUV 多層膜反射鏡的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Thermal control and ultralow-expansion substrate” determines the key performance of “EUV multilayer mirrors”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"每片鏡子吸收約 30% 的 EUV 以及光源帶來的紅外與帶外輻射，鏡面溫度會上升並隨曝光負載變化。基板採用 ULE 或 Zerodur 等超低膨脹玻璃陶瓷，熱膨脹係數在 ±20 ppb/K 以內，再配合主動溫控、熱感測與模型補償，才能把熱致面形漂移壓在次奈米。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「熱控與低膨脹基板」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Each mirror absorbs about 30% of the EUV plus infrared and out-of-band radiation from the source, so its temperature rises and varies with exposure load. Substrates use ultralow-expansion glass ceramics such as ULE or Zerodur with thermal expansion within ±20 ppb/K, combined with active temperature control, thermal sensing and model-based compensation, to keep thermal figure drift sub-nanometre. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Thermal control and ultralow-expansion substrate”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：一維熱變形 Δh ≈ α·ΔT·h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A one-dimensional thermal deformation is Δh ≈ α·ΔT·h.","failure":"常見誤解：「超低膨脹材料就表示熱變形為零。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Ultralow-expansion material means zero thermal deformation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「熱控與低膨脹基板」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Thermal control and ultralow-expansion substrate”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-25-k1","title":"熱負載、低膨脹材料與面形漂移","titleEn":"Thermal load, ultralow-expansion materials and figure drift","text":"每片鏡子吸收約 30% 的 EUV 以及光源帶來的紅外與帶外輻射，鏡面溫度會上升並隨曝光負載變化。基板採用 ULE 或 Zerodur 等超低膨脹玻璃陶瓷，熱膨脹係數在 ±20 ppb/K 以內，再配合主動溫控、熱感測與模型補償，才能把熱致面形漂移壓在次奈米。","textEn":"Each mirror absorbs about 30% of the EUV plus infrared and out-of-band radiation from the source, so its temperature rises and varies with exposure load. Substrates use ultralow-expansion glass ceramics such as ULE or Zerodur with thermal expansion within ±20 ppb/K, combined with active temperature control, thermal sensing and model-based compensation, to keep thermal figure drift sub-nanometre.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：超低膨脹材料就表示熱變形為零。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Ultralow-expansion material means zero thermal deformation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「熱負載、低膨脹材料與面形漂移」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Thermal load, ultralow-expansion materials and figure drift\" is correct?","options":["超低膨脹材料就表示熱變形為零。","每片鏡子吸收約 30% 的 EUV 以及光源帶來的紅外與帶外輻射，鏡面溫度會上升並隨曝光負載變化。","每片鏡子都通過驗收，整組光學就自動合格。"],"optionsEn":["Ultralow-expansion material means zero thermal deformation.","Each mirror absorbs about 30% of the EUV plus infrared and out-of-band radiation from the source, so its temperature rises and varies with exposure load.","If every mirror passes, the assembled optics automatically pass."],"answer":1,"explanation":"每片鏡子吸收約 30% 的 EUV 以及光源帶來的紅外與帶外輻射，鏡面溫度會上升並隨曝光負載變化。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Each mirror absorbs about 30% of the EUV plus infrared and out-of-band radiation from the source, so its temperature rises and varies with exposure load. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"a402-v12-26","title":"熱負載、低膨脹材料與面形漂移：定量估算","titleEn":"Thermal load, ultralow-expansion materials and figure drift: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「熱控與低膨脹基板」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Thermal control and ultralow-expansion substrate” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：一維熱變形 Δh ≈ α·ΔT·h。取 α = 10 ppb/K、鏡體厚度 h = 50 mm、局部溫升 ΔT = 0.2 K，Δh ≈ 1×10⁻⁸×0.2×0.05 m = 0.1 nm；若改用 CTE 為 0.5 ppm/K 的普通玻璃，同樣條件下變形達 5 nm。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A one-dimensional thermal deformation is Δh ≈ α·ΔT·h. With α = 10 ppb/K, a 50 mm mirror body and a local rise ΔT = 0.2 K, Δh ≈ 1×10⁻⁸×0.2×0.05 m = 0.1 nm; an ordinary glass with CTE 0.5 ppm/K would deform 5 nm under the same conditions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：以已知熱負載照射或加熱鏡面並同時量面形，比較量測漂移與有限元素或一維估計值；檢查 CTE 在鏡體內的均勻性是否足以解釋殘差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Irradiate or heat the mirror with a known load while measuring figure, compare the measured drift with finite-element or one-dimensional estimates, and check whether CTE homogeneity across the blank explains any residual.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"一維熱變形 Δh ≈ α·ΔT·h。取 α = 10 ppb/K、鏡體厚度 h = 50 mm、局部溫升 ΔT = 0.2 K，Δh ≈ 1×10⁻⁸×0.2×0.05 m = 0.1 nm；若改用 CTE 為 0.5 ppm/K 的普通玻璃，同樣條件下變形達 5 nm。","textEn":"A one-dimensional thermal deformation is Δh ≈ α·ΔT·h. With α = 10 ppb/K, a 50 mm mirror body and a local rise ΔT = 0.2 K, Δh ≈ 1×10⁻⁸×0.2×0.05 m = 0.1 nm; an ordinary glass with CTE 0.5 ppm/K would deform 5 nm under the same conditions.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「熱負載、低膨脹材料與面形漂移」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Thermal load, ultralow-expansion materials and figure drift\", which statement holds?","options":["雙層數越多，反射率一定越高。","基板很厚時，幾百奈米薄膜的應力可以忽略。","一維熱變形 Δh ≈ α·ΔT·h。"],"optionsEn":["More bilayers always give higher reflectance.","For a thick substrate the stress of a few hundred nanometres of film is negligible.","A one-dimensional thermal deformation is Δh ≈ α·ΔT·h."],"answer":2,"explanation":"一維熱變形 Δh ≈ α·ΔT·h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A one-dimensional thermal deformation is Δh ≈ α·ΔT·h. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"a402-v12-27","title":"熱負載、低膨脹材料與面形漂移：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Thermal load, ultralow-expansion materials and figure drift: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「熱控與低膨脹基板」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Thermal control and ultralow-expansion substrate” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"以已知熱負載照射或加熱鏡面並同時量面形，比較量測漂移與有限元素或一維估計值；檢查 CTE 在鏡體內的均勻性是否足以解釋殘差。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Irradiate or heat the mirror with a known load while measuring figure, compare the measured drift with finite-element or one-dimensional estimates, and check whether CTE homogeneity across the blank explains any residual. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：基板 CTE 不均勻時，即使平均 CTE 為零，溫度場仍會造成非均勻變形，出現無法用整體溫控消除的像散。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: With inhomogeneous CTE, a zero average CTE still leaves non-uniform deformation under a temperature field, producing astigmatism that global temperature control cannot remove.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以已知熱負載照射或加熱鏡面並同時量面形，比較量測漂移與有限元素或一維估計值；檢查 CTE 在鏡體內的均勻性是否足以解釋殘差。","textEn":"Irradiate or heat the mirror with a known load while measuring figure, compare the measured drift with finite-element or one-dimensional estimates, and check whether CTE homogeneity across the blank explains any residual.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-27-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「熱負載、低膨脹材料與面形漂移」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Thermal load, ultralow-expansion materials and figure drift\"?","options":["以已知熱負載照射或加熱鏡面並同時量面形，比較量測漂移與有限元素或一維估計值；檢查 CTE 在鏡體內的均勻性是否足以解釋殘差。","量測時不必記錄溫度、振動與時間等條件，因為它們不會影響結果。","在真空中工作的鏡面不會受到污染。"],"optionsEn":["Irradiate or heat the mirror with a known load while measuring figure, compare the measured drift with finite-element or one-dimensional estimates, and check whether CTE homogeneity across the blank explains any residual.","Temperature, vibration and timing need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A mirror working in vacuum cannot get contaminated."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以已知熱負載照射或加熱鏡面並同時量面形，比較量測漂移與有限元素或一維估計值；檢查 CTE 在鏡體內的均勻性是否足以解釋殘差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Irradiate or heat the mirror with a known load while measuring figure, compare the measured drift with finite-element or one-dimensional estimates, and check whether CTE homogeneity across the blank explains any residual. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"a402-v12-28","title":"熱負載、低膨脹材料與面形漂移：失效診斷","titleEn":"Thermal load, ultralow-expansion materials and figure drift: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「熱控與低膨脹基板」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Thermal control and ultralow-expansion substrate” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"基板 CTE 不均勻時，即使平均 CTE 為零，溫度場仍會造成非均勻變形，出現無法用整體溫控消除的像散。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"With inhomogeneous CTE, a zero average CTE still leaves non-uniform deformation under a temperature field, producing astigmatism that global temperature control cannot remove. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：基板採用 ULE 或 Zerodur 等超低膨脹玻璃陶瓷，熱膨脹係數在 ±20 ppb/K 以內，再配合主動溫控、熱感測與模型補償，才能把熱致面形漂移壓在次奈米。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Substrates use ultralow-expansion glass ceramics such as ULE or Zerodur with thermal expansion within ±20 ppb/K, combined with active temperature control, thermal sensing and model-based compensation, to keep thermal figure drift sub-nanometre.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「超低膨脹材料就表示熱變形為零。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Ultralow-expansion material means zero thermal deformation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"基板 CTE 不均勻時，即使平均 CTE 為零，溫度場仍會造成非均勻變形，出現無法用整體溫控消除的像散。","textEn":"With inhomogeneous CTE, a zero average CTE still leaves non-uniform deformation under a temperature field, producing astigmatism that global temperature control cannot remove.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱負載、低膨脹材料與面形漂移」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Thermal load, ultralow-expansion materials and figure drift\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自操作人員失誤，系統設計不需要檢討。","基板 CTE 不均勻時，即使平均 CTE 為零，溫度場仍會造成非均勻變形，出現無法用整體溫控消除的像散。","每片鏡子都通過驗收，整組光學就自動合格。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is operator error, so the system design never needs review.","With inhomogeneous CTE, a zero average CTE still leaves non-uniform deformation under a temperature field, producing astigmatism that global temperature control cannot remove.","If every mirror passes, the assembled optics automatically pass."],"answer":1,"explanation":"基板 CTE 不均勻時，即使平均 CTE 為零，溫度場仍會造成非均勻變形，出現無法用整體溫控消除的像散。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"With inhomogeneous CTE, a zero average CTE still leaves non-uniform deformation under a temperature field, producing astigmatism that global temperature control cannot remove. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"a402-v12-29","title":"鏡組整合、對準與驗收：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Mirror-set integration, alignment and acceptance: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-28"],"objective":"說明「系統對準與驗收報告」如何決定EUV 多層膜反射鏡的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “System alignment and acceptance record” determines the key performance of “EUV multilayer mirrors”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"反射鏡以撓性或運動學支撐安裝，避免夾持應力並允許微米到奈米級的位置調整；每片鏡子的位移與傾斜對波前的靈敏度由光學設計的靈敏度矩陣給出。最後以成像或波前系統量測、眩光量測與壽命外推共同構成驗收，而不是只看元件各自合格。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「系統對準與驗收報告」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Mirrors are held on flexure or kinematic mounts that avoid clamping stress and allow micrometre-to-nanometre adjustment; the wavefront sensitivity to each mirror's displacement and tilt comes from the optical design's sensitivity matrix. Acceptance combines system wavefront or imaging measurement, flare measurement and lifetime extrapolation rather than separate component passes. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “System alignment and acceptance record”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：若某鏡傾斜靈敏度為 0.5 nm 波前／µrad，允許該項佔用 0.2 nm 預算，則傾斜公差為 0.4 µrad；對 200 mm 跨距，相當於邊緣位移 80 nm，顯示對準機構需要奈米級解析度。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: If a mirror's tilt sensitivity is 0.5 nm wavefront per µrad and the item is allowed 0.2 nm of budget, the tilt tolerance is 0.4 µrad; over a 200 mm span that equals 80 nm of edge displacement, showing that the alignment mechanism needs nanometre resolution.","failure":"常見誤解：「每片鏡子都通過驗收，整組光學就自動合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If every mirror passes, the assembled optics automatically pass.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「系統對準與驗收報告」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “System alignment and acceptance record”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-29-k1","title":"鏡組整合、對準與驗收","titleEn":"Mirror-set integration, alignment and acceptance","text":"反射鏡以撓性或運動學支撐安裝，避免夾持應力並允許微米到奈米級的位置調整；每片鏡子的位移與傾斜對波前的靈敏度由光學設計的靈敏度矩陣給出。最後以成像或波前系統量測、眩光量測與壽命外推共同構成驗收，而不是只看元件各自合格。","textEn":"Mirrors are held on flexure or kinematic mounts that avoid clamping stress and allow micrometre-to-nanometre adjustment; the wavefront sensitivity to each mirror's displacement and tilt comes from the optical design's sensitivity matrix. Acceptance combines system wavefront or imaging measurement, flare measurement and lifetime extrapolation rather than separate component passes.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：每片鏡子都通過驗收，整組光學就自動合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If every mirror passes, the assembled optics automatically pass. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鏡組整合、對準與驗收」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Mirror-set integration, alignment and acceptance\" is correct?","options":["每片鏡子都通過驗收，整組光學就自動合格。","只要材料夠純、夠透明，EUV 也能像 DUV 一樣用透鏡成像。","反射鏡以撓性或運動學支撐安裝，避免夾持應力並允許微米到奈米級的位置調整；每片鏡子的位移與傾斜對波前的靈敏度由光學設計的靈敏度矩陣給出。"],"optionsEn":["If every mirror passes, the assembled optics automatically pass.","With pure enough transparent material, EUV could be imaged with lenses like DUV.","Mirrors are held on flexure or kinematic mounts that avoid clamping stress and allow micrometre-to-nanometre adjustment."],"answer":2,"explanation":"反射鏡以撓性或運動學支撐安裝，避免夾持應力並允許微米到奈米級的位置調整；每片鏡子的位移與傾斜對波前的靈敏度由光學設計的靈敏度矩陣給出。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Mirrors are held on flexure or kinematic mounts that avoid clamping stress and allow micrometre-to-nanometre adjustment; the wavefront sensitivity to each mirror's displacement and tilt comes from the optical design's sensitivity matrix. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"a402-v12-30","title":"鏡組整合、對準與驗收：定量估算","titleEn":"Mirror-set integration, alignment and acceptance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「系統對準與驗收報告」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “System alignment and acceptance record” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：若某鏡傾斜靈敏度為 0.5 nm 波前／µrad，允許該項佔用 0.2 nm 預算，則傾斜公差為 0.4 µrad；對 200 mm 跨距，相當於邊緣位移 80 nm，顯示對準機構需要奈米級解析度。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: If a mirror's tilt sensitivity is 0.5 nm wavefront per µrad and the item is allowed 0.2 nm of budget, the tilt tolerance is 0.4 µrad; over a 200 mm span that equals 80 nm of edge displacement, showing that the alignment mechanism needs nanometre resolution. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：用靈敏度矩陣把量到的 Zernike 項反解成各鏡的位移與傾斜修正量，施加修正後再量一次，確認殘差收斂並在預算內；驗收報告需同時列出反射率、波前、眩光、污染衰減速率與熱漂移。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Invert the measured Zernike terms through the sensitivity matrix into per-mirror displacement and tilt corrections, apply them, re-measure, and confirm the residual converges within budget; the acceptance record must list reflectance, wavefront, flare, contamination decay rate and thermal drift together.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"若某鏡傾斜靈敏度為 0.5 nm 波前／µrad，允許該項佔用 0.2 nm 預算，則傾斜公差為 0.4 µrad；對 200 mm 跨距，相當於邊緣位移 80 nm，顯示對準機構需要奈米級解析度。","textEn":"If a mirror's tilt sensitivity is 0.5 nm wavefront per µrad and the item is allowed 0.2 nm of budget, the tilt tolerance is 0.4 µrad; over a 200 mm span that equals 80 nm of edge displacement, showing that the alignment mechanism needs nanometre resolution.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鏡組整合、對準與驗收」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Mirror-set integration, alignment and acceptance\", which statement holds?","options":["若某鏡傾斜靈敏度為 0.5 nm 波前／µrad，允許該項佔用 0.2 nm 預算，則傾斜公差為 0.4 µrad。","達到可見光光學的光滑度，對 EUV 也足夠。","在真空中工作的鏡面不會受到污染。"],"optionsEn":["If a mirror's tilt sensitivity is 0.5 nm wavefront per µrad and the item is allowed 0.2 nm of budget, the tilt tolerance is 0.4 µrad.","A surface smooth enough for visible optics is smooth enough for EUV.","A mirror working in vacuum cannot get contaminated."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若某鏡傾斜靈敏度為 0.5 nm 波前／µrad，允許該項佔用 0.2 nm 預算，則傾斜公差為 0.4 µrad；對 200 mm 跨距，相當於邊緣位移 80 nm，顯示對準機構需要奈米級解析度。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"If a mirror's tilt sensitivity is 0.5 nm wavefront per µrad and the item is allowed 0.2 nm of budget, the tilt tolerance is 0.4 µrad; over a 200 mm span that equals 80 nm of edge displacement, showing that the alignment mechanism needs nanometre resolution. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"a402-v12-31","title":"鏡組整合、對準與驗收：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Mirror-set integration, alignment and acceptance: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「系統對準與驗收報告」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “System alignment and acceptance record” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"用靈敏度矩陣把量到的 Zernike 項反解成各鏡的位移與傾斜修正量，施加修正後再量一次，確認殘差收斂並在預算內；驗收報告需同時列出反射率、波前、眩光、污染衰減速率與熱漂移。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Invert the measured Zernike terms through the sensitivity matrix into per-mirror displacement and tilt corrections, apply them, re-measure, and confirm the residual converges within budget; the acceptance record must list reflectance, wavefront, flare, contamination decay rate and thermal drift together. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：安裝時的夾持力或黏著劑收縮會把合格的鏡面壓出像散；若驗收只核對元件報告而不做系統量測，這類錯誤會留到曝光結果才被發現。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Clamping force or adhesive shrinkage during mounting can press astigmatism into a passing mirror; acceptance that only checks component reports without a system measurement leaves such errors to be found in exposure results.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用靈敏度矩陣把量到的 Zernike 項反解成各鏡的位移與傾斜修正量，施加修正後再量一次，確認殘差收斂並在預算內；驗收報告需同時列出反射率、波前、眩光、污染衰減速率與熱漂移。","textEn":"Invert the measured Zernike terms through the sensitivity matrix into per-mirror displacement and tilt corrections, apply them, re-measure, and confirm the residual converges within budget; the acceptance record must list reflectance, wavefront, flare, contamination decay rate and thermal drift together.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-31-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鏡組整合、對準與驗收」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Mirror-set integration, alignment and acceptance\"?","options":["沿用另一台設備或另一個案例的量測結果，就可視為本系統已完成驗證。","用靈敏度矩陣把量到的 Zernike 項反解成各鏡的位移與傾斜修正量，施加修正後再量一次，確認殘差收斂並在預算內。","λ/4 的面形品質對任何波長都是「繞射極限」。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another instrument or another case counts as verifying this system.","Invert the measured Zernike terms through the sensitivity matrix into per-mirror displacement and tilt corrections, apply them, re-measure, and confirm the residual converges within budget.","λ/4 figure quality is diffraction limited at any wavelength."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用靈敏度矩陣把量到的 Zernike 項反解成各鏡的位移與傾斜修正量，施加修正後再量一次，確認殘差收斂並在預算內；驗收報告需同時列出反射率、波前、眩光、污染衰減速率與熱漂移。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Invert the measured Zernike terms through the sensitivity matrix into per-mirror displacement and tilt corrections, apply them, re-measure, and confirm the residual converges within budget; the acceptance record must list reflectance, wavefront, flare, contamination decay rate and thermal drift together. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"a402-v12-32","title":"鏡組整合、對準與驗收：失效診斷","titleEn":"Mirror-set integration, alignment and acceptance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"prerequisiteIds":["a402-v12-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「系統對準與驗收報告」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “System alignment and acceptance record” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"安裝時的夾持力或黏著劑收縮會把合格的鏡面壓出像散；若驗收只核對元件報告而不做系統量測，這類錯誤會留到曝光結果才被發現。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Clamping force or adhesive shrinkage during mounting can press astigmatism into a passing mirror; acceptance that only checks component reports without a system measurement leaves such errors to be found in exposure results. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：最後以成像或波前系統量測、眩光量測與壽命外推共同構成驗收，而不是只看元件各自合格。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Acceptance combines system wavefront or imaging measurement, flare measurement and lifetime extrapolation rather than separate component passes.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「每片鏡子都通過驗收，整組光學就自動合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If every mirror passes, the assembled optics automatically pass.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a402-v12-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"安裝時的夾持力或黏著劑收縮會把合格的鏡面壓出像散；若驗收只核對元件報告而不做系統量測，這類錯誤會留到曝光結果才被發現。","textEn":"Clamping force or adhesive shrinkage during mounting can press astigmatism into a passing mirror; acceptance that only checks component reports without a system measurement leaves such errors to be found in exposure results.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]},{"id":"a402-v12-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鏡組整合、對準與驗收」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Mirror-set integration, alignment and acceptance\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["調高增益或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數異常。","只要材料夠純、夠透明，EUV 也能像 DUV 一樣用透鏡成像。","安裝時的夾持力或黏著劑收縮會把合格的鏡面壓出像散；若驗收只核對元件報告而不做系統量測，這類錯誤會留到曝光結果才被發現。"],"optionsEn":["Raising the gain or widening the acceptance limits solves most anomalies.","With pure enough transparent material, EUV could be imaged with lenses like DUV.","Clamping force or adhesive shrinkage during mounting can press astigmatism into a passing mirror."],"answer":2,"explanation":"安裝時的夾持力或黏著劑收縮會把合格的鏡面壓出像散；若驗收只核對元件報告而不做系統量測，這類錯誤會留到曝光結果才被發現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Clamping force or adhesive shrinkage during mounting can press astigmatism into a passing mirror; acceptance that only checks component reports without a system measurement leaves such errors to be found in exposure results. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4}],"sourceIds":["v8b-lenses","v12o-zeiss-smt-litho-optics","v12o-cxro-multilayer"],"curriculumVersion":12,"stepCount":32,"estimatedMinutes":800}};
